lesson: 118
title: Two steps and a number you do not need
stars: 1
explain: Some stories give a number that does not help answer the question. Read the question first, then pick only the numbers it needs.
explain: «Tom is 9. He has 5 boxes of 8 crayons and gives away 12 crayons. How many crayons are left?» His age does not matter.
explain: Step one: 5 × 8 = 40 crayons. Step two: 40 - 12 = 28 crayons left.
vars: a=name b=name t=thing p=3..8 c=4..12 g=2..30 x=2..12 y=7..11
need: g < p * c
need: x != p && x != c
answer: p * c - g
exercise: {a} is {y} years old. {a.He} has {p} boxes with {c} crayons in each box. {a.He} gives away {g} crayons. How many crayons does {a.he} have left?
exercise: {a} buys {p} packs of {c} {t}. Each pack costs {x} dollars. {a.He} gives {g} {t} to {b}. How many {t} does {a} keep?
exercise: A class has {p} rows of {c} chairs. {x} of the children wear glasses. {g} chairs are taken away. How many chairs are still there?
exercise: There are {p} shelves with {c} books on each shelf. The library opens at {y} o'clock. {g} books are lent out. How many books are still on the shelves?
exercise: {a} has {p} bags with {c} marbles in each. {a.His} friend {b} has {x} bags. {a} loses {g} marbles. How many marbles does {a} have now?
exercise: A farmer puts {c} eggs in each of {p} baskets. He has {x} cows. He sells {g} eggs. How many eggs are left in the baskets?
test: On a bus with {x} windows there are {p} rows of seats, {c} seats in each row. {g} seats are taken. How many seats are free?
test: {a}, who is {y} years old, keeps {t} in {p} boxes, {c} in each box. {g} of them are given away. How many {t} remain?
test: {b} walked {x} km to the shop and bought {p} cartons of {c} juice boxes. On the way home {b.he} drank or shared {g} of them. How many juice boxes are left?
test: A garden has {p} beds with {c} plants in each bed. It rained for {x} days, and then {g} plants died. How many plants are still growing?
exercise: {a} lives in Texas and is {y}. {a.He} has {p} boxes of crayons, {c} crayons per box, and hands out {g} crayons to {a.his} class. How many crayons remain?
exercise: How many {t} does {a} still have? {a.He} bought {p} packs with {c} {t} apiece for {x} dollars a pack, then gave {g} {t} to {b}.
exercise: A school in Manchester has {p} rows of {c} desks. The school is {x} miles from the station. {g} desks are carried out. How many desks are still in the rows?
exercise: In a library in Melbourne, every one of {p} shelves holds {c} books. The library closes at {y} o'clock. {g} books are borrowed. How many books remain on the shelves?
exercise: {a}, aged {y}, owns {p} bags of marbles with {c} in every bag. {b} owns {x} bags. {a} loses {g} marbles. How many marbles has {a} got left?
exercise: On a farm in Iowa a farmer fills {p} baskets with {c} eggs each. The farm has {x} pigs. {g} eggs are sold at the market. How many eggs are still in the baskets?
exercise: {p} trays, {c} cupcakes per tray, {x} candles on the table: {g} cupcakes are eaten. How many cupcakes are left?
exercise: {a} is {y.words} years old and lives in Wellington, {x} km from the sea. For a party {a.he} ties {c} balloons in each of {p} bunches. {g} balloons pop. How many balloons have not popped?
test: A ferry in Sydney Harbour has {x} lifebuoys and {p} rows of {c} seats. {g} of the seats are taken. How many seats are empty?
test: How many stamps are left in {b}'s album? It had {p} pages with {c} stamps per page, {b} is {y} years old, and {b.he} swapped away {g} stamps.
test: {a} paid {x} dollars for each of {p} boxes of {c} doughnuts in Boston. {g} doughnuts were eaten on the way home. How many doughnuts got home?
test: In an orchard near Dublin there are {p} rows with {c} apple trees per row. {x} of the workers are new. {g} trees are cut down. How many apple trees remain?
test: {b} is {y}. {b.He} has {p} tins of {c} biscuits and {x} cousins. After {g} biscuits are eaten, how many biscuits are left in the tins?
test: A Toronto hotel has {p} floors with {c} rooms on every floor and {x} lifts. {g} rooms are booked. How many rooms are not booked?
