exam: It is given that {a}, aged {y} years, is in possession of {p} boxes, each containing {c} crayons, of which {g} crayons are subsequently given away. Determine the number of crayons remaining in the possession of {a}.
exam: Pursuant to a purchase of {p} packs of {c} {t} at a cost of {x} dollars per pack, {a} transfers {g} {t} to {b}. Ascertain the number of {t} retained by {a}.
exam: A classroom is furnished with {p} rows of {c} chairs; {x} pupils therein wear spectacles. Whereas {g} chairs are subsequently removed, state the number of chairs that remain.
exam: Compute the number of {t} remaining in respect of {a}, given that {a.he} acquired {p} packets of {c} {t} each, paid {x} dollars per packet, and thereafter relinquished {g} {t}.
exercise: {a}'s old cat was put to sleep at {y} years old, so {a.he} gives away its toys. There were {p} boxes of {c} toy mice, and {a.he} gives {g} of them to {b}. How many toy mice are left?
exercise: After the shop's "restructuring", {x} workers were let go. The shop still has {p} shelves with {c} {t} on each, and it sells {g} {t}. How many {t} are left on the shelves?
test: {b} "borrowed" {g} of my {t}, yeah right, bloody thief. i had {p} packs of {c}, paid {x} dollars a pack. how many i got left
